  'sb.h1a': 'Meet your AI', 'sb.h1b': 'Strategy Builder.',
  'sb.heroBody': 'Describe your strategy in plain English. Tradvio AI writes the code, backtests it instantly against real market data, and deploys it live. Build, test, and launch - no coding required.',
  'sb.cta1': 'Try Free - No Card Needed', 'sb.cta2': 'How it works',
  'sb.p1': 'No coding required', 'sb.p2': 'Instant backtesting', 'sb.p3': 'Deploy in minutes',
  'sb.chatTitle': 'AI Strategist', 'sb.online': 'ONLINE',
  'sb.userMsg': 'Build me a strategy: RSI below 30 with MACD bullish crossover. 2% stop-loss, 4% take-profit, BTC/USD 1H.',
  'sb.aiTitle': 'Strategy generated',
  'sb.aiMsg1': 'I\'ve created', 'sb.aiMsg2': 'Conditions: RSI(14) < 30, MACD(12,26,9) bullish cross. Stop 2%, target 4%. Want me to run a backtest on the last 90 days?',
  'sb.validated': 'Validated',
  'sb.btl1': 'Return (90d)', 'sb.btl2': 'Win rate', 'sb.btl3': 'Max drawdown',
  'sb.railsEyebrow': 'AI with rails',
  'sb.rails1': 'Three failure modes', 'sb.rails2': 'of AI-only trading.',
  'sb.ftEyebrow': 'Features',
  'sb.ft1': 'AI that understands', 'sb.ft2': 'trading.',
  'sb.f1t': 'Natural language', 'sb.f1d': 'Describe your strategy in plain English. The AI translates it into clean, executable code - no programming required.',
  'sb.f2t': 'Instant backtesting', 'sb.f2d': 'One-click testing on real market data. See returns, win rate, and drawdown before you risk a penny.',
  'sb.f3t': 'Strategy conversion', 'sb.f3d': 'Already have a Pine Script or MQL5 strategy? The AI converts it automatically with full backtesting support.',
  'sb.f4t': 'Chart analysis', 'sb.f4d': 'Upload chart screenshots and the AI analyses the patterns - then builds a strategy around what it sees.',
  'sb.f5t': 'Real market data', 'sb.f5d': 'Attach live candle data from supported exchanges and platforms. Every backtest runs on real spreads and slippage.',
  'sb.f6t': 'Version control', 'sb.f6d': 'Every edit creates a new version. Compare, restore, or fork strategies - your full history is always safe.',
  'sb.hiwEyebrow': 'How it works',
  'sb.hiw1': 'From idea to live strategy', 'sb.hiw2': 'in four steps.',
  'sb.sp1t': 'Describe your idea', 'sb.sp1d': 'Tell the AI your indicators, conditions, and risk rules - in plain English.',
  'sb.sp2t': 'Review the code', 'sb.sp2d': 'The AI generates clean, editable code. Review it in the built-in editor.',
  'sb.sp3t': 'Backtest instantly', 'sb.sp3d': 'Run a quick test or a full backtest with custom dates and real market data.',
  'sb.sp4t': 'Deploy live', 'sb.sp4d': 'Save your strategy, connect your platform, and put it to work.',
  'sb.ewEyebrow': 'Built for every trader',
  'sb.ew1': 'Whether you code', 'sb.ew2': 'or not.',
  'sb.n1t': 'No-code trading', 'sb.n1d': 'Go from idea to working strategy without writing a single line of code. The AI handles the technical side.',
  'sb.n2t': 'Strategy migration', 'sb.n2d': 'Bring your Pine Script or MQL5 strategies. The AI converts them automatically with full backtesting support.',
  'sb.n3t': 'Rapid prototyping', 'sb.n3d': 'Test dozens of variations in minutes. Tweak a parameter, rerun the backtest, compare results side by side.',
  'sb.st1': 'Markets supported', 'sb.st2': 'Asset classes', 'sb.st3': 'To first backtest', 'sb.st4': 'AI available',
  'sb.faqEyebrow': 'FAQ',
  'sb.faq1': 'AI strategy builder', 'sb.faq2': 'questions.',
  'sb.fq1': 'Do I need to know how to code?', 'sb.fa1': 'No. Describe your strategy in plain English and the AI writes the code for you. The generated code stays visible and editable in the built-in editor - so you can learn from it or tweak it anytime.',
  'sb.fq2': 'Does AI trade for me?', 'sb.fa2': 'No. The AI builds strategies - it does not execute trades autonomously. You review the code, validate the backtest, and decide when to deploy. You stay in control at every step.',
  'sb.fq3': 'Can I edit what the AI builds?', 'sb.fa3': 'Yes. Every strategy opens in the same visual builder and code editor. Change indicators, adjust risk rules, or rewrite logic - your strategy, your way.',
  'sb.fq4': 'Can AI run a backtest for me?', 'sb.fa4': 'Yes. One click runs your strategy against historical data. The AI explains the results - returns, win rate, drawdown - and suggests changes to improve performance.',
  'sb.fq5': 'What if AI makes a bad strategy?', 'sb.fa5': 'You don\'t deploy it. Backtest results, version control, and live monitoring decide quality. Every strategy must prove itself on historical data before it goes near a live market.',
  'sb.fq6': 'Which markets can I build strategies for?', 'sb.fa6': 'Stocks, crypto, forex, commodities, indices, ETFs, and CFDs - over 1,600 markets with institutional-grade historical data for backtesting.',
  'sb.fm1p': 'AI alone', 'sb.fm1t': 'Hallucinated functions', 'sb.fm1d': 'Ask an LLM to "write a trading strategy" and it invents functions, parameters, and indicators that don\'t exist. The result looks right and trades wrong.', 'sb.fm1s': 'With Tradvio AI', 'sb.fm1sd': 'The AI is constrained to a validated component system. Every output is structurally correct - indicators, sizing, risk rules, and costs all built in.',
  'sb.fm2p': 'AI without backtests', 'sb.fm2t': 'A guess in disguise', 'sb.fm2d': 'Untested strategies are guesses dressed up as recommendations. Without historical validation, you\'re flying blind.', 'sb.fm2s': 'With Tradvio AI', 'sb.fm2sd': 'Backtest as a portfolio with real fees, slippage, and funding. Your strategy must prove itself on data before deployment.',
  'sb.fm3p': 'AI without ownership', 'sb.fm3t': 'Black-box signals', 'sb.fm3d': 'Black-box signals leave you no leverage when market conditions change. You can\'t edit what you can\'t see.', 'sb.fm3s': 'With Tradvio AI', 'sb.fm3sd': 'Edit, fork, version, and iterate. The strategy is yours - every line of code visible and modifiable.',
  'sb.close1': 'Start with an idea.', 'sb.close2': 'We\'ll help you prove it.',
  'sb.closeSub': 'You don\'t need a perfect plan - just an idea worth testing. Most traders have a working backtest within 10 minutes.',
  'sb.closeCta': 'Start Building →',
  'sb.closeNote': 'Backtesting uses historical data. Past performance does not guarantee future results. Trading involves risk - only trade with capital you can afford to lose.',
